# Serving contract style context

RS-GOV-04: `src/lib.rs` permits `clippy::result_large_err` because the adapter propagates
eprfs-core's `TreeError`, including its inline CID and path. Boxing only in this adapter
would introduce a second error representation for the same refusal. The tradeoff is a larger
return value. Evidence and the underlying decision: `../eprfs-core/.epr-meta`, “structured
refusals by value”; regression command: `just gate eprfs`. Responsible: eprfs-serve maintainers.
Revisit when TreeError's representation changes or measured serving costs justify indirection.
